.Dd September 22, 2026
.Dt MIROTALK 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mirotalk
.Nd administer the MiroTalk SFU service on FreeBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm service
.Cm mirotalk
.Ar start | stop | restart | status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This installation of MiroTalk SFU was built using the HARDENED build option.
It provides the customizable and privacy-hardened FreeBSD configuration layer.
To build the standard MiroTalk version instead, select the STANDARD build option when configuring the port, then rebuild and reinstall it.
.Pp
The HARDENED build only supports self-hosted, open-source, administrator-controlled infrastructure.
Upstream integrations that depend on third-party-controlled services are disabled in this build and are not exposed as supported configuration.
.Pp
The
.Nm
port installs MiroTalk SFU under
.Pa %%WWWDIR%%
and integrates it with the FreeBSD rc system.
Enable it with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirotalk_enable="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
The rc.conf interface is intentionally limited to service
execution:
.Bl -tag -width "mirotalk_daemon_group"
.It Va mirotalk_enable
Enable the service.  Default:
.Dq NO .
.It Va mirotalk_daemon_user
Service user passed to
.Xr daemon 8 .  Default:
.Dq www .
.It Va mirotalk_daemon_group
Group used for the service runtime and log directories.  Default:
.Dq www .
.El
.Sh APPLICATION CONFIGURATION
Use
.Xr mirotalk.conf 5
for deployment, site, and supported upstream environment settings.
The application configuration code at
.Pa %%WWWDIR%%/app/src/config.js
is package-owned and is replaced on upgrades.
Do not edit it to configure the service.
If an earlier HARDENED installation left a customized
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/config.js ,
compare it with the new configuration and move needed supported settings to
.Pa mirotalk.conf .
.Sh SITE ASSETS
Site-owned logos and other presentation files may be stored in
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/site-assets
and are served under
.Pa /site-assets/ .
The administrator-owned
.Pa site.css
is loaded after MiroTalk's own stylesheets so local CSS can adjust such things
as logo dimensions without patching package-owned CSS.
.Pp
The unauthenticated
.Pa /about
page identifies the site and upstream open-source software and provides the
Corresponding Source link for the exact FreeBSD package revision.
.Sh LOCAL USERS
Local authentication is enabled by default in
.Xr mirotalk.conf 5 .
The account database is
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/users
and should be owned by
.Li root:wheel
with mode 0600.
.Pp
Each account occupies one line with four fields separated by
.Ql | :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
username | password | display name | allowed rooms
.Ed
.Pp
Whitespace around fields is ignored.
Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.Ql #
are ignored.
The
.Ql |
character and newline cannot occur in a field.
The allowed-rooms field is either
.Ql *
or a JSON array of exact meeting keys.
For example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fred    | H7mQ9kR4WxPc | Fred Bloggs | *
mary    | N8vK2pT7YsQa | Mary Smith  | ["staff", "weekly"]
.Ed
.Pp
A template is installed as
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/users.sample .
.Sh JWT SECRET

On first start the rc script creates
.Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/jwt-secret
from 32 bytes of kernel-provided random data.
The resulting 256-bit secret is root-owned, mode 0600, and reused on later
starts.
MiroTalk consumes it during configuration and removes
.Ev JWT_SECRET
from the Node process environment.
.Sh LOGGING
Standard output and error are written to
.Pa /var/log/mirotalk/mirotalk.log .
The package installs a
.Xr newsyslog 8
configuration to rotate this log rather than retaining it indefinitely.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "%%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/mirotalk.conf.sample"
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/mirotalk.conf
Deployment and site configuration.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/mirotalk.conf.sample
Package-provided deployment example.
.It Pa %%WWWDIR%%/app/src/config.js
Package-owned application configuration code.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/users
Root-only local user database.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/users.sample
Example local user database.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/site-assets
Site-owned presentation assets.
.It Pa %%PREFIX%%/etc/mirotalk/jwt-secret
Automatically generated JWT signing secret.
.It Pa /var/run/mirotalk
Runtime state and pid file.
.It Pa /var/log/mirotalk/mirotalk.log
Service log.
.El
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The HARDENED changes, administrator choices, and audit limits are documented in
.Pa %%DOCSDIR%%/HARDENING.md .
.Pp
The files
.Pa users
and
.Pa jwt-secret
contain secrets and should remain root-owned mode 0600.
.Pp
.Pa mirotalk.conf
is read as configuration data by MiroTalk and is not executed as shell code.
Do not place user passwords or the JWT secret in it or in
.Pa rc.conf .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mirotalk.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr service 8
.Sh PRIVACY
MiroTalk's upstream privacy page describes an upstream deployment and is not assumed to describe this FreeBSD installation.
A site privacy policy is optional and is configured with
.Va PRIVACY_POLICY_NAME
or
.Va PRIVACY_POLICY_URL
in
.Pa @ETCDIR@/mirotalk.conf .
If neither is configured, the user interface does not display a Privacy Policy link.

.Sh SITE COPYRIGHT
Site-specific material may have a different copyright owner from the MiroTalk
software.  Set
.Va SITE_COPYRIGHT
in
.Pa @ETCDIR@/mirotalk.conf
to display an optional site copyright notice in the login footer and local
About page.  MiroTalk software attribution, copyright, license, and
Corresponding Source information remain on the About page.
